# Architecture

Follow `.cursor/rules/workflow.mdc` before any non-trivial change (read docs/rules first; update docs after structural or convention changes).

Read `docs/architecture.md` first. The codebase is the source of truth for what exists. That doc separates **Current implementation** from **Project standard**. Do not treat a standard as a folder or route that already exists.

## Do not change the architecture

Never change the existing project architecture unless the user explicitly asks for an architectural change.

Prefer extending the existing structure. Never move/rename layers for taste. Do not replace the router, TanStack Query, the Zustand theme store, or ConnectRPC.

## Layers

```text
app → features → infrastructure / shared
```

| Area | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `src/app/` | Shell: layouts (`pageFrame`), providers, route table |
| `src/features/` | Business domains (only `auth` exists today) |
| `src/infrastructure/` | Shared `config/transport.ts` + Connect clients (`auth/`, …) |
| `src/shared/` | Reused UI, theme, tokens, LoadingPage, NotFoundPage |

- No business forms in `app/routes`.
- `src/App.tsx` is the Vite render root, not a feature page.
- Add `admin` / `agent` / `member` / `reseller` only when implementing that feature.

## Current routes (do not invent others)

All routes are in `src/app/routes/index.tsx`:

- `/login` → lazy default-export `LoginPage` + Suspense `LoadingPage`
- `*` → lazy default-export `NotFoundPage` + Suspense `LoadingPage`

There is no `/` → `/login` redirect today. `/` hits `*`.

## Naming

- Follow existing file names and folders (including current spellings such as `ToggleThem`, `Loadingpage.tsx`). Do not rename unless asked.
- Hooks: `useSomething.ts`. Schemas: `SomethingSchema.ts`.
- No `common/`, `misc/`, `helpers/`, `temp/`, `new/`.

## Related rules

- Theme: `theme.mdc` — no theme script in `index.html`
- API: `connectrpc-bff.mdc`
- UI: `react-ui.mdc` (Login is the visual reference)
- Workflow: `workflow.mdc`
